<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="25665b6">&lt;p&gt;
    Project teams should confirm that all project participants and stakeholders agree that:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The project was completed
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The project met its objectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Lessons learned were documented
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Open issues/risks (if any) were communicated
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Follow-up activities or future projects were identified and communicated
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    There are seven procedures for closing a project - six performed sequentially and the seventh is performed throughout
    the entire process for closing a project.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Start closing a project:&lt;/strong&gt; Enable the project structure to&amp;nbsp;verify the project team has the
        necessary items it needs for closing a project. This includes identifying stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Conduct Lessons Learned Session:&lt;/strong&gt; Collect project successes and areas for improvement so that
        future projects can benefit from this experience. The approval for the Project Lessons Learned Report is decided by
        the Managing Project Sponsor. The approval decision must be one of two approval options:&lt;br /&gt;
        1)Yes (Project Lessons Learned Report is accepted) or, 2) Need More Information (Project Lessons Learned Report is
        approved in principle, but put on hold pending additional action and/or submission of additional information).
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Prepare and socialize Project Closure Report:&lt;/strong&gt; The Project Manager analyzes the final results of
        the project and compares it to the approved baseline.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Determine approval of Project Closure Report:&lt;/strong&gt; The Project Closure Report is reviewed by the
        Managing Project Sponsor to make a decision on the Project Closure Report. The approval decision must be one of two
        approval options:1) Yes (approve Project Closure Report) or, 2) Need More Information (return Project Closure
        Report with a request for more information).
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Provide Project Resource Feedback:&lt;/strong&gt; The Project Manager provides feedback on each project team
        resource.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Complete closing a project:&lt;/strong&gt; Bring all work that is performed during this process group to closure.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Monitor and measure closing a project:&lt;/strong&gt; The procedures for closing a project are monitored and
        tracked against predefined&lt;br /&gt;
        performance targets.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
